// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`prompt snapshots > content pass, chunk 0 1`] = `
"You are writing one region of a dungeon: six rooms and everything in them.

WHAT YOU ARE GIVEN
Every room, entity, connector, and creature has already been decided by procgen.
Counts and hit dice are already rolled. Your job is to realise it in prose and
settle the few things procgen leaves to you -- not to choose what is there. Each
line lists the rolled keywords behind it as table=value; those are seeds to
realise, not text to echo.

PER ROOM
- name + base: the room's standing description. base is IMMUTABLE -- only what is
  true of the place itself, not what a party is doing in it, nothing that changes
  when its contents change.
- Each listed entity's name + base, written the same way: fixed identity, concrete
  to this fiction.
- Each connector: name + what it physically IS -- a door, a stair, a corridor, a
  crawl, a short drop, a collapsed arch, whatever separates the two rooms, even if
  mundane. For a GATED connector also write what blocks it, seen from this room;
  do not invent the key.
- Promotable details: a detail is always part of the room's description. Make it
  its own entity ONLY if a player would act on it. Most stay as description.

CREATURES -- CONSOLIDATE
The count is already rolled. A mass of one creature type is ONE entity with a
single stat block; do NOT split it into individuals. "5 x rank-and-file" is one
entity you name in the plural ("Fen-seals") and write once. Only a specimen
marked "distinct" -- an elite, a named person -- becomes its own entity alongside
the mass. Write the group's shared base once (the mass); write each distinct
specimen its own base. Give the mass and each distinct one a one-line current
activity fitting the encounter. Stats: you are given the hit-dice spine; return
only DEVIATIONS the keywords imply (a heavier die for claws, armour, a morale or
ability shift). Leave stats out for an average body.

THE GOAL
One room is marked GOAL. Create exactly one entity that embodies the objective. Read the fiction and decide what type it needs to be -- an Item, a RoomFeature, or a Creature -- so that a party acting on it plausibly satisfies the mission. Then name and write it.

HARD RULES
1. Every listed entity, connector, and encounter must appear exactly once. Do not
   add a creature, hazard, or connector that was not listed.
2. Keywords are seeds, not labels. Realise them into the place; do not gloss.
3. Do not contradict the fiction. Material, history, and the state of the ruin are
   settled.
4. Depth and tension are tone, never content. A calm room holding a lethal thing
   still holds it.
5. A clue must point at what it is said to point at, written as something noticed.

MAKE THEM DISTINCT
These rooms are read in sequence. Give each one something the others lack. If two
would read the same, change one.

=== DUNGEON FICTION (shared context) ===
[dungeon context]

=== ROOMS TO WRITE (6) ===

--- room_0 ---
identity: Well
role: goal
depth: furthest   tension: lethal
headline: special
room keywords: Room=Well
entity [<id>] reward (Item): Valuable Material=Signet ring
connector [<id>] to room_1 CONCEALED -- write it as the thing a person would walk past -- a seam, a draught, a panel that rings hollow -- not as a door; no barrier
connector [<id>] to room_4 -- say what it physically is; no barrier
GOAL HERE: reward "Jewels" + mission "Deface".
  Create exactly one entity that embodies the objective. Read the fiction and decide what type it needs to be -- an Item, a RoomFeature, or a Creature -- so that a party acting on it plausibly satisfies the mission. Then name and write it.
open exits: room_1, room_4

--- room_1 ---
identity: Storeroom
depth: furthest   tension: lethal
headline: creature
room keywords: Room=Storeroom  |  Room Detail=Unusual smell
entity [<id>] reward (Item): Valuable Material=Buried cache
promotable detail [Room Detail=Unusual smell] -- make it an entity only if a player would act on it
connector [<id>] to room_2 -- say what it physically is; no barrier
encounter [mob_6vw_2] Solo, unaffiliated, currently Question, disposition hostile
    distinct named [<id>] (leader) -> its own entity  [background=Alchemist  |  Asset=Powerful spouse  |  Liability=Jealous  |  Method=Alchemy  |  Appearance=Sinewy  |  Personality=Serene  |  Goal=Revenge  |  Reputations=Proper  |  Mannerisms=Flowery speech  |  Hobbies=Archaeology]
      PEOPLE GROUP, tier Solo
        faction: Hired killers
        traits: Pious; Cowardly
        - [LEADER] Odette (female) [<id>]; background: Alchemist; asset: Powerful spouse; liability: Jealous; method: Alchemy; appearance: Sinewy; personality: Serene; goal: Revenge; Reputations: Proper; Mannerisms: Flowery speech; Hobbies: Archaeology
open exits: room_0, room_2

--- room_2 ---
identity: Courtyard
depth: deep   tension: uneasy
headline: quiet
room keywords: Room=Courtyard  |  Room Detail=Furniture
entity [<id>] clue (RoomFeature): Clue=Moisture -- points at creatures in an adjoining room (room_1)
promotable detail [Room Detail=Furniture] -- make it an entity only if a player would act on it
connector [<id>] to room_3 -- say what it physically is; no barrier
open exits: room_1, room_3

--- room_3 ---
identity: Gate house
depth: middle   tension: dangerous
headline: creature
room keywords: Room=Gate house
connector [<id>] to room_4 -- say what it physically is; no barrier
connector [<id>] to room_5 -- say what it physically is; no barrier
encounter [mob_6vw_1] Solo, base of group 1, currently Negotiate, disposition hostile
    mass: 1 x rank-and-file -> ONE consolidated entity, one stat block  [Complexity=major  |  Silhouette=humanoid  |  Trait=Ethereal  |  Ability=Camouflaging; Gaze weapon; Teleporting  |  Feature=Fur  |  Mutation=Extra eyes  |  Tactic=Demand duel  |  Personality=Bored  |  Weakness=Phylactery, Flowers]
      MONSTER GROUP, tier Solo
        base: major humanoid; trait: Ethereal; ability: Camouflaging; ability: Gaze weapon; ability: Teleporting; feature: Fur; mutation: Extra eyes; tactic: Demand duel; personality: Bored; weakness: Phylactery, Flowers
open exits: room_2, room_4, room_5

--- room_4 ---
identity: Oubliette
depth: deep   tension: uneasy
headline: special
room keywords: Room=Oubliette
entity [<id>] obstacle (RoomFeature): Obstacle=Bridge  |  Cairn Feature=Repels
entity [<id>] reward (RoomFeature): Knowledge=Instructions
open exits: room_3, room_0

--- room_5 ---
identity: Chasm
role: entrance
depth: threshold   tension: calm
headline: none
room keywords: Room=Chasm
entity [<id>] entrance (RoomFeature): Entrance=Tree roots
open exits: room_3

=== RESPONSE FORMAT ===
Return JSON only, no prose outside it:

{
  "rooms": [
    {
      "ref": "<room ref, exactly as given>",
      "name": "<short room name>",
      "base": "<the room's standing description>",
      "entities": [ { "ref": "<entity ref>", "name": "<name>", "base": "<identity>" } ],
      "promotions": [ { "text": "<detail text as given>", "name": "<name>", "base": "<identity>", "hidden": false } ],
      "connectors": [ { "ref": "<connector ref>", "name": "<name>", "form": "<what it physically is>", "requirement": "<gated only: what blocks it>" } ],
      "encounters": [
        {
          "ref": "<encounter ref>",
          "group": { "name": "<plural name>", "base": "<shared identity>", "activity": "<one line>", "stats": { "damage": "1d8" } },
          "distinct": [
            { "kind": "elite|named", "member": "<named: person id>", "name": "<name>", "base": "<identity>", "isLeader": false, "activity": "<one line>", "stats": { "armorDefense": 14 } }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "goal": { "entityType": "Item|RoomFeature|Creature", "name": "<name>", "base": "<identity>" }
    }
  ]
}

Include each key only when the room has it; "group" only when a mass is listed;
"distinct" only for specimens marked distinct; omit "goal" except in the GOAL
room. Leave "stats" out for an average creature."
`;

exports[`prompt snapshots > dungeon pass 1`] = `
"You are establishing a dungeon's standing fiction, before any of its rooms are
written. Everything below has already been rolled. Your job is to make one
coherent place out of it -- not to choose what is there, and not to describe any
individual room.

Whatever you write here is read by every later pass and cannot be contradicted
afterwards. Commit to it.

WHAT TO WRITE

name        What this place is called. Short. It may be what its builders called
            it, or what people call it now -- pick whichever the fiction earns.

theme       The sensory register, in a few sentences: what it is built from,
            what the light is like, what it sounds like, what it smells of, what
            the air does. Concrete nouns. This is the palette every room draws
            from, so make it specific enough to constrain and broad enough to
            furnish twenty rooms.

history     What the place was for, what happened to it, and how it came to hold
            what it holds now. Tie the ruination cause to the inhabitants: the
            best dungeons are one story, not a building plus some monsters that
            wandered in. A few short paragraphs.

goal        You are given a Dungeon Reward and a Mission. Resolve them into ONE
            objective -- take one, discard the other, or fuse them, whichever
            reads best. Then write it twice:
              summary: one line the player is told before they go in.
              spec:    what actually counts as achieving it, for the referee.
                       Concrete enough to adjudicate: what must be found, done,
                       taken, or ended. This decides when the run is won, so do
                       not leave it to taste.

opening     What the player reads standing at the threshold, before the first
            room. Second person. The approach, the way in, and the first thing
            the place does to them. A short paragraph -- it sets the register
            for everything after it.

groups      For each listed group id, a plural name and a standing base.
            The base is what these things ARE, permanently and everywhere in
            this dungeon: their form, their nature, how they behave, what they
            want. Realise the rolled keywords into a creature or a faction; do
            not list the keywords back.
            Write nothing that a single encounter could change. No "currently",
            no "at the moment", no room, no posture, no wound. Twelve instances
            of this group in eight rooms all share this one description, so
            anything true of only one of them does not belong in it.
            A group's LEADER and any named people get their own descriptions
            later -- write the group here, not its individuals.

HARD RULES
1. Do not contradict the rolls. Form, ruination, inhabitants and goal seed are
   settled; you are realising them, not revising them.
2. Do not write rooms. No room names, no floor plan, no "in the eastern wing".
   Rooms are written later, by a pass that has the layout in front of it.
3. Return a base for every listed group id and for no other id.
4. Keywords are seeds, not vocabulary. "Fungal" means work out what the fungus
   has done to them; it does not mean using the word "fungal".
5. Write prose, not notes. This is read as fiction by everything downstream.

=== DUNGEON BLUEPRINT SEED ===
id: dungeon_rx   seed: 1005   size: 1   level: 1

PURPOSE
  Form (original purpose): Hotel
  Built by: Heretical Monks

RUINATION
  Ruined: YES
  Condition: Overpopulated   (also seeds initial dungeon state)
  Cause: Natural Erosion   (seeds history)

INHABITANTS (1 group)
  --- Group 1: MONSTERS / Tier: Solo  [<id>] ---
    Complexity: major
    Silhouette: humanoid
    Humanoid seed (Trait): Ethereal
    Traits/Abilities: Ability: Camouflaging; Ability: Gaze weapon; Ability: Teleporting
    Features/Mutations: Feature: Fur; Mutation: Extra eyes
    Tactic: Demand duel
    Weakness: Phylactery; Flowers
    Personality: Bored  (discard if not intelligent enough)

PLAYER GOAL SEED
  Dungeon Reward: Jewels
  Mission: Deface
  (pick one, discard the other, or combine -- whichever reads best)

=== GROUPS YOU MUST WRITE (1) ===
One name + base for each id below, exactly these ids and no others. They are
the groups printed above; the id is in brackets on each group's header line.
  <id>

=== RESPONSE FORMAT ===
Return JSON only, no prose outside it:

{
  "name": "<the dungeon's name>",
  "theme": "<sensory register: material, light, sound, smell, air>",
  "history": "<what it was, what happened, who is here now>",
  "goal": {
    "summary": "<one line, told to the player>",
    "spec": "<what counts as achieving it, for the referee>"
  },
  "openingProse": "<second person, at the threshold, before the first room>",
  "groups": [
    { "id": "<exactly as listed>", "name": "<plural name>", "base": "<standing identity>" }
  ]
}"
`;
